#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# number_expand

#% text
# `number_expand(x)` gives the digits of `x` times their place values: `number_expand(157)` is `[100, 50, 7]`. `number_expand(x, b)` expands in base `b`, `number_expand(x, b, len)` into `len` terms, the last holding the rest.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A fractional part stays in the last term; complex numbers expand real and imaginary parts together.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
number_expand(157)
#% output
#= [100, 50, 7]

#% cell
number_expand(157, 2)
#% output
#= [128, 0, 0, 16, 8, 4, 0, 1]

#% cell
number_expand(157, 2, 3)
#% output
#= [128, 0, 29]

#% cell
number_expand(1111/7, 2)
#% output
#= [128, 0, 0, 16, 8, 4, 2, 5/7]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `number_compose`, `integer_digits`
